---
// FAQ section — no props needed
---

<section id="faq" class="faq-section reveal">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Common Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>
          Is Buddy really local-first?
          <svg class="summary-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes. All your files, reading logs, drawing canvases, and notes are saved directly to your hard drive. Your data never leaves your machine.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          Which AI providers does Buddy support?
          <svg class="summary-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Buddy is Bring-Your-Own-Key. It works with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Ollama, and dozens of other cloud or local AI providers through a flexible configuration.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          How can I extend Buddy's capabilities?
          <svg class="summary-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Connect custom Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, add reusable skill bundles, or register new shell tools directly to expand what Buddy can do.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          How does Buddy guide my learning?
          <svg class="summary-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Buddy uses proven educational frameworks like Bloom's Taxonomy and active recall. It guides you through reasoning with Socratic-style questions rather than simply giving you answers.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style is:global>
  /* === FAQ === */
  .faq-section {
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
  }

  .faq-list {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  details {
    background-color: var(--color-card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.2s var(--ease-out), box-shadow 0.2s var(--ease-out);
  }

  details:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-card-hover-border);
  }

  details[open] {
    border-color: rgba(255, 107, 0, 0.3);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(255, 107, 0, 0.05);
  }

  summary {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    user-select: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .summary-icon {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    transition: transform 0.25s var(--ease-out);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  details[open] summary .summary-icon {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    max-height: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 250ms var(--ease-out), opacity 250ms var(--ease-out), padding 250ms var(--ease-out);
    padding: 0 20px;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    border-top: 1px solid transparent;
    max-width: 65ch;
    will-change: max-height;
  }

  details[open] .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 20px 16px 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
</style>

<script>
  // FAQ accordion with smooth height animation
  document.querySelectorAll("details").forEach((el) => {
    const summary = el.querySelector("summary")
    const answer = el.querySelector(".faq-answer") as HTMLElement

    if (summary && answer) {
      summary.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        e.preventDefault()
        if (el.hasAttribute("open")) {
          // Close: animate then remove open
          answer.style.maxHeight = "0px"
          answer.style.opacity = "0"
          setTimeout(() => {
            el.removeAttribute("open")
          }, 250)
        } else {
          // Open: set open, then animate
          el.setAttribute("open", "")
          // Force reflow so transition triggers
          void answer.offsetHeight
          answer.style.maxHeight = `${answer.scrollHeight}px`
          answer.style.opacity = "1"
        }
      })
    }
  })
</script>
